{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>She is brought out, and she sent.</b> Her heart did not falter from striving to vindicate herself even though they were bringing her out to be burned, for her heart was like the heart of a lion." "<b>To the man to whom these belong.</b> Even though she was in mortal danger, she did not wish to shame him in public, as the Sages of blessed memory said: It is better for a person to cast himself into a fiery furnace than to shame his fellow in public — they derived this from Tamar (Sotah 10b)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:52.023627706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}